# Focused P01 final evidence PRE repair — exact method, no product authority

This additive repair retains the original execution plan and FAIL report unchanged. Existing accepted P01 task2.4/2.5 scope, three exceptions, guide1.0/tokens1.0.0 and STOP rules remain unchanged. No implementation until fresh independent PRE PASS. No new production selector/property/callback/API/vendor/routing change is authorized. Original plan applies except that steps2–3 are now concretely defined below. Human372PNG manifest acceptance remains NOT_APPROVED; no cumulative PASS/archive/P02.

## Packet completeness repair

Include original transition receipt, all three current compatibility E2E files (workbench-multiroot.spec.ts, diagrams.spec.ts, bundle-flows.spec.ts), all543 raw current root source files and all1971 saved fresh root artifacts with their original manifests. Include full pinned app.min.js, vendor manifest/index/grapheditor/high-contrast CSS and sprite bitmap. The full app.min.js contains original Toolbar/Actions/Menus code and actual Editor.*Image data resources; no edited excerpts stand in for it. Review can reproduce audit2, source/artifact hashes and permitted old callback preservation. Keep original PRE101events/17receipts/FAIL exactly; revised packet selection is recorded explicitly. No foreign worktree files.

## Enabled-state provenance and fixed control inventory

Run original diagramFixture('frame', {mode,density}) six times (Light/Dark/HC x compact/comfortable), untouched original launch/configure/capture/KA/open/font/paint/revision helper. Capture every connected visible original upper .geToolbarContainer control and every paint-bearing descendant/pseudo (bounds, styles, image/SVG/background/mask, disabled attr, aria-disabled, mxDisabled, own enabled boolean). Preserve hidden controls as HIDDEN records; unknown mappings are NOT_MEASURED, never an exclusion. No clicks/mutating actions after ready; read original __p01Ui only. Semantic XML/preferences/selection/history/viewport/currentPage/file hashes and UI/graph/toolbar/frame identity must remain unchanged through observation.

Pinned Toolbar.prototype.init/addItems/addItem maps zoomIn/zoomOut/undo/redo/delete/toFront/toBack/fillColor/strokeColor/shadow/insertFreehand/generate to Editor image constants and live actions. Predeclare this exact ordered mapping; verify actual title equals unique live action getTitle plus original shortcut formatting, resource equals corresponding Editor.*Image, and disabled attribute agrees with actual action.enabled (the original addItem callback uses enabled, not opacity). Log isEnabled separately; disagreement/unknown => NOT_MEASURED. Menu controls are viewPanels/edgeShape/edgeStyle/insert/layout: original addMenu/menuCreated/addMenuHandler checks own element.enabled (undefined is permitted by original click guard), live menu.enabled and mxDisabled. Match original constant/resource/title and require agreement. Shapes clone/table dropdown or unknown controls remain separately documented and unmeasured unless original exact source and actual capability establish mapping; do not classify all geButton enabled by CSS alone. All measured enabled icons use threshold3:1 (A11Y-002); proven disabled excluded only from applicable contrast verdict and raw record retained.

## Predeclared actual glyph sampling, no CSS foreground proxy

1. Save untouched full page PNG with Electron screenshot at actual DPR1, viewport1280x850, default zoom, actual ready fonts/two paints. Preserve frame/toolbar/control rectangles and raw original resource strings/bytes. Read an original background/img resource via isolated image decode to off-DOM canvas to retain its actual RGBA alpha mask and natural size; preserve original resource plus decode RGBA/hash. This canvas never modifies the visible UI. Data URI bytes decoded exactly; protocol asset fetch is owner read of pinned local app resource. SVG remains original bytes plus browser decoded natural raster, with decoder/browser version recorded.
2. Initially support only a single image/background resource with integer natural dimensions, no repeat, computed background-size auto or exact integer pixel dimensions, integer CSS destination origin and DPR1 scale1, identity transform, no CSS filter (none), opacity1 on every ancestor, no mask/mix-blend/backdrop-filter/shadow layer, and uniform opaque effective backdrop. Preserve actual values for unsupported filters/scales/fractional positions/layers; report NOT_MEASURED rather than approximate. CSS background-position resolves against actual padding-box and image dimensions by standard percentage/px formula; require integer placement and known border/padding/background-origin/clip. IMG uses actual content rectangle/intrinsic dimensions/object-fit mapping with same restrictions. Never recolor/filter the source or screenshot. Unsupported cases are blocking coverage, not filtered PASS.
3. Define foreground-core mask BEFORE observations: original decoded alpha exactly255 and all four cardinal neighbors alpha255; erode by one pixel to exclude antialias edges. Retain every core coordinate; sample the corresponding raw full screenshot pixel centers after fixed resource->control->frame->page placement. No color-based/favorable pixel selection. Zero core pixels => NOT_MEASURED. Define backdrop mask: alpha0 pixel and all four cardinal neighbors alpha0 within same resource destination; retain every coordinate, require nonempty and one exact opaque screenshot RGB value which agrees with recorded effective backdrop. Nonuniform/overlaid background, occlusion, partial clipping, missing glyph/placement resource or unprovable composition => NOT_MEASURED. Direct embedded SVG paint without a reproducible corresponding resource mask is also NOT_MEASURED; no invented CSS-color PASS.
4. For every core coordinate compute WCAG relative-luminance contrast of actual screenshot RGB versus the proven backdrop RGB. Preserve all raw RGBs, coordinates, resource/screenshot hashes, formula, min/max/count and full per-pixel contrasts, not just passing samples. Every nominal foreground-core pixel of an enabled mapped glyph must be >=3; any lower measurement is deterministic FAIL. Disabled raw measurements still saved but never waive enabled results. No rounding/tolerance changes or fringe counting. A screenshot has actual paint: inherited CSS color is metadata only. If all measured core pixels match backdrop, contrast1 is valid measured failure only with independently proven source/placement/capability; otherwise NOT_MEASURED.
5. Before trusting measurement, isolated in-memory PNG/RGBA tests exercise known opaque foreground/background pass, black-on-black fail, disabled exclusion plus enabled counterexample, antialias-only/zero-core rejection, wrong source/placement/layer NOT_MEASURED, and snapshot immutability. Fixtures cannot become production assets. Save positive and negative raw reports, exact code/commands, original helper AST text/hash/locations. No production fixture/import/testAPI or dependency installation.

## Consequences

This bounded method may prove an enabled defect even while other controls remain unmeasured. Never claim whole A11Y coverage/P01 PASS from a subset. Unknown/unsupported enabled paint must remain BLOCKED for final closure and may require a separate precisely reviewed diagnostic extension. If deterministic defect is measured, preserve RED and RCA; only existing approved test paths may receive meaningful append-only regression after PRE, with old raw prefix/callbacks preserved. Product repair requiring new img/background/filter selectors/properties must STOP for the exact human UI scope decision. Do not infer permission from the review or invent a fourth exception. Keep current root valid for existing oracles; changed permanent source would reopen3.1 and all source-bound runtime/root bindings. Existing FUI POST PASS and all historical FAIL remain.
The requestSha256 in selection.json is the exact preliminary request before attaching selection.json itself. It is historical draft identity, not final dispatched request identity. Shared same-run input/request/control/receipt hashes bind the final request. This note explicitly retains the draft bytes and prevents a self-referential request digest claim.
